1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,464
The second attempt began with a bit of routine maintenance and a kilo of new cable.

2
00:00:04,464 --> 00:00:14,387
Its power came from a smaller motor, a quieter drive, and an electronic mixture of sensors that could be arranged in any order.

3
00:00:14,387 --> 00:00:21,086
“If the component fails, the whole activity stops,” the engineer said.

4
00:00:21,086 --> 00:00:24,085
“That is the point.”

5
00:00:24,085 --> 00:00:33,128
The concert in the park, the bush beside the path, and the script of the presentation were all part of the same routine.

6
00:00:33,128 --> 00:00:39,967
The intensity of the mechanical work was low; the intensity of the mathematics was not.

7
00:00:39,967 --> 00:00:50,160
A trigger in the software, a hook in the interface, and a chaos of small updates had to be replaced by feedback.

8
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:58,463
The laser scanned the surface, the gravity sensor dipped, and the suspension of the scan was logged twice.

9
00:00:58,463 --> 00:01:03,467
“Consistency is not repetition,” the analyst said.

10
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:20,049
“A repeated test that changes nothing proves nothing.” An odor of burnt plastic, a graphic of the new methodology, and a projector that erased a digit: the lab was learning to trust its own instruments.

11
00:01:20,049 --> 00:01:25,733
The voltage had to be upgraded before the consolidation of the two servers.

12
00:01:25,733 --> 00:01:38,935
An elimination of three old linkages, a cohesion of the remaining ones, and a relativity of standards between the two labs made the merge slower than anyone expected.

13
00:01:38,935 --> 00:01:50,787
As an end to the attempt, they arranged one public session: a pull of the plug, a message on the screen, and a current of questions from the audience.

14
00:01:50,787 --> 00:01:54,707
“We can enable the exit,” Maya said.

15
00:01:54,707 --> 00:02:06,779
“We cannot enable the trust.” It was a level of honesty that the training had not prepared them for, and they waited at the end of the day for the result.

16
00:02:06,779 --> 00:02:20,941
The mile of cable, the wait of a week, and the pick of the third option were, in the end, the same decision: to keep the system small enough to be explained by the person it remembers.

17
00:02:20,941 --> 00:02:27,125
It was an attempt at something small, and the training had prepared them for none of it.

18
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:35,933
The current had turned; the force of the argument was on their side, and they could enable the end they wanted without a fight.

19
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:46,881
A capture of one screen and a consolidate of two registers: the last step was to make the record smaller than the thing it described.
